course: dictionary
lesson: 2561
title: Delicate: easily damaged, fine, or needing care
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Delicate is a describing word, and it can mean several things. The context tells you which meaning fits. «Ears are delicate: the tiny hair cells inside never grow back, so a ringing in your ears after a bang is a warning.» Here delicate means easily hurt, so your ears need protecting.
explain: «Goggles are worn in the school lab because eyes are delicate and some chemicals damage them in seconds.» The reason after because gives the clue: delicate means something that is easily damaged. Always ask what the sentence needs, then swap your meaning in to check it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can describe fine things, soft tastes, or tricky situations. «Instruments are delicate and often expensive: you carry them in their case.» Here delicate means easily broken, so it needs gentle handling, not just a pretty look.
fact: Delicate means easily broken or damaged, so it needs gentle care.
fact: Delicate can also mean fine, thin or light, like lace or a butterfly's wings.
fact: A delicate taste, colour or smell is soft and not strong.
fact: «A delicate situation» needs careful handling so nobody is upset.
fact: «Feeling delicate» in Britain is a polite way to say hungover.
exercise: «Instruments are delicate and often expensive: you carry them in their case.» What does delicate mean here? | Cheap and heavy | Happy and full of song | *Easily damaged, so they need careful handling | Very loud and bright
exercise: «Her cake had a delicate taste, light and not too sweet.» What does delicate taste mean? | *Soft and not strong | Burnt and bitter | Sour and sticky | Very spicy and hot
exercise: Chloe says, «Handle it with care, this is a delicate matter.» What does a delicate matter mean? | A maths homework sum | A game with lots of rules | *A problem that needs careful, tactful handling | A thing that is very heavy
test: «Small birds have very delicate lungs, so a good owner watches them closely.» Why does the owner watch them closely? | Because birds like to be watched | Because birds sing at night | Because the birds are very big | *Because their lungs can be easily harmed
test: «The lace was so delicate that it tore when Mum touched it.» What does delicate mean? | Thick and strong | Dirty and wet | *Fine and easily torn | Loud and bright
exam: «Feeling delicate» is a polite British way to say what? | Cold from the snow | Very strong and healthy | Sleepy after a long day | *Hungover
